A||||3||BroCar 87||Rims and Tires   ?? 84 SE and 87 coupe||||5||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||08-12-2000||11:33 PM||||Alright. I have an 84 SE and an 87 Coupe. The rims look the same, yet the tires on the SE are P215, and the ones on my Coupe are P195. I know I have the WS6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> suspension on the SE, but could I put those rims and tires on my coupe, or is there not enough suspension room or something. The SE rims and tires look bigger, yet the tires are both for the 14 inch rims.<BR>so my question is CAN I go wider or is it the special suspension on the SE that allows it to do so??<BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||08-12-2000||11:37 PM||||My 85SE had 195/14's on it and when I bought new tires I added 215's and had no problems at all. You should be fine.<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||08-12-2000||11:50 PM||||just like you, i have an '87 coupe and a '84 (actually two) that came with ws6 susp. and larger section width tires. the rims were all the same though, except white on my indy. i don't think you'll have a problem. right now my '87 has much larger tires and rims (16x7.5, with 225 and 255/50- 16 tires, coilovers needed on rear). <P>some may say thats too much tire, but i'm just saying they'll fit. i plan to get the same rims for all 3 cars. may stay with 225/50's all around though on the others.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-13-2000||01:20 PM||||The 87 should have 6" wide 14" rims. You can mount any tire that is rated for that width of rim. You must check the tire makers data sheets to see what rim a particular tire fits since every brand/type of tire is differant. Not all 215's are going to be rated for a 6" rim. Much of this data is online.<P>Keep in mind that section width is not tread width. Tread width IS NOT printed on the tire. Tread width for a given size tire can vary more than 1 inch. (Example a 190 tire may have tread width from 5.5 to nearly 7 inches.) because of that a 205 or even 215 may not be as much wider than a 190 as you think.||||reg||1
